#grungetext([#title("A Thunderous Prelude to Slaughter")])
_by The Storyteller_
#thin_line

The night before, you each have nightmares of thunder, rain, and battle. When *_Odo knows the worst is coming, he will call upon Tor's aid._* He sacrifices his new wife and his chandler, among others, leaving their smoking bodies in his courtyard as a warning to his enemies. He begins with 2 favor, and will gain 1 more for each significant sacrifice he manages to make.

#text(size: 1.5em)[#align(center)[#uses(4)]]

For each favor, pick one thing you dream of in the night:
- *Strength in Battle:* Adamantios's muscles bulging and sparking with lightning, fury in his eyes.
- *The Cost of Betrayal:* Heavy rain falls on Gordin's delve, washing away blood, washing away bodies, flooding the mines --- The GM picks one of the Political results to be reduced by one.
- *Ruin of his Enemies:* He knows the architects of his ruin, and he will make them pay --- Stonetop becomes beset by drought.
- *Power! Unlimited Power!* Not gaining enough of what he seeks from Tor, he secretly makes some of his sacrifices to one of the Things Below, gaining great power at heavy cost.

*The power of the sacrifice is the cost to the person making it:*
If you sacrifice someone to Tor, reduce Odo's favor by 1 and add 1d6 to the Revolution dice pool.
If your sacrifice is of someone you know well or love, or otherwise fucked up, reduce Odo's favor by 2 and add 2d6 to the Revolution dice pool.

